---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
---

<Layout lang="en" title="Terms of Service | BrewMind" description="Terms of Service for the BrewMind app and website.">
  <Header />
  <main class="pt-24 pb-16 px-6">
    <article class="max-w-3xl mx-auto prose">
      <h1>Terms of Service</h1>

      <h2>1. Scope</h2>
      <p>
        These Terms of Service (&ldquo;Terms&rdquo;) govern your access to and use of the BrewMind mobile application (&ldquo;App&rdquo;) and the BrewMind website at <a href="https://brewmind.app">brewmind.app</a> (&ldquo;Website&rdquo;), both operated by Tegrovio &mdash; Dominik Palzer, Sterntalerweg 65, 40235 D&uuml;sseldorf, Germany (&ldquo;we&rdquo;, &ldquo;us&rdquo;, &ldquo;our&rdquo;).
      </p>
      <p>
        By installing the App or using the Website you agree to these Terms. If you do not agree, please do not use the App or Website.
      </p>

      <h2>2. Account Requirement</h2>
      <p>
        Use of the App requires the creation of a personal user account with a valid e-mail address and a password. You are responsible for keeping your credentials confidential and for all activities that occur under your account. Please notify us immediately at <a href="mailto:hello@brewmind.app">hello@brewmind.app</a> if you suspect unauthorised access.
      </p>

      <h2>3. Cloud Sync</h2>
      <p>
        When signed in, the App synchronises your brew data (espresso parameters, equipment, feedback) with our cloud infrastructure (Supabase, EU region) to enable backup and cross-device access. This synchronisation is a core function of the App and cannot be disabled while your account is active.
      </p>
      <p>
        All data is stored exclusively in the EU. For details on what is synchronised and how it is protected, please refer to our <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>4. Beta Status</h2>
      <p>
        The App is currently provided as <strong>beta software</strong>. This means:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Features, functionality, and design may change at any time without prior notice.</li>
        <li>The App may contain bugs, errors, or interruptions in service.</li>
        <li>We do not guarantee uninterrupted availability of the App or cloud services.</li>
        <li>Beta access is provided free of charge and may be discontinued or transitioned to a paid model in the future.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>5. No Warranty</h2>
      <p>
        The App and Website are provided <strong>&ldquo;as is&rdquo; and &ldquo;as available&rdquo;</strong> without warranties of any kind, express or implied, including but not limited to warranties of merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose, or non-infringement. We do not warrant that the App will be error-free, secure, or continuously available.
      </p>
      <p>
        We are not liable for any loss of data, loss of brew records, or other damages arising from the use of the App, to the extent permitted by applicable law.
      </p>

      <h2>6. Termination and Account Deletion</h2>
      <p>
        You may stop using the App at any time. You can delete your account directly within the App. Upon account deletion all server-side data associated with your account is permanently and irreversibly erased. See our <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>, Section&nbsp;12 for details.
      </p>
      <p>
        We reserve the right to suspend or terminate accounts that violate these Terms or applicable law.
      </p>

      <h2>7. User Obligations</h2>
      <p>
        When using the App and Website you agree not to:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Reverse-engineer, decompile, or disassemble the App or any part thereof.</li>
        <li>Access or attempt to access other users&rsquo; data.</li>
        <li>Use the App or Website for any unlawful purpose or in violation of applicable regulations.</li>
        <li>Attempt to overload, disrupt, or compromise our infrastructure or cloud services.</li>
        <li>Resell, sublicense, or redistribute access to the App without our express written consent.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>8. Changes to These Terms</h2>
      <p>
        We may update these Terms from time to time. Material changes will be communicated to users with an active account by e-mail at least 14 days before taking effect. Continued use of the App after that date constitutes acceptance of the revised Terms. The current version is always available at <a href="/terms">brewmind.app/terms</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>9. Governing Law and Jurisdiction</h2>
      <p>
        These Terms are governed exclusively by the laws of the Federal Republic of Germany, excluding its conflict-of-law provisions. The United Nations Convention on Contracts for the International Sale of Goods (CISG) does not apply.
      </p>
      <p>
        The place of jurisdiction for all disputes arising from or in connection with these Terms is D&uuml;sseldorf, Germany, to the extent permitted by law.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you are a consumer resident in the European Union you may also bring proceedings before the courts of your country of residence.
      </p>

      <h2>10. Contact</h2>
      <p>
        For questions regarding these Terms, please contact us at:<br />
        <a href="mailto:hello@brewmind.app">hello@brewmind.app</a>
      </p>
      <p>
        Tegrovio &mdash; Dominik Palzer<br />
        Sterntalerweg 65<br />
        40235 D&uuml;sseldorf, Germany
      </p>
    </article>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Layout>

<style>
  .prose {
    line-height: 1.75;
  }
  .prose h1 {
    font-size: 2rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
    color: var(--color-text);
  }
  .prose h2 {
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    margin-top: 2rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
    color: var(--color-text);
  }
  .prose h3 {
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
    color: var(--color-text);
  }
  .prose p {
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }
  .prose ul {
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    padding-left: 1.5rem;
    list-style-type: disc;
  }
  .prose li {
    margin-bottom: 0.25rem;
  }
  .prose a {
    color: var(--color-primary);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 2px;
  }
  .prose a:hover {
    color: var(--color-primary-light);
  }
  .prose strong {
    color: var(--color-text);
  }
  .prose code {
    background: var(--color-surface);
    padding: 0.15rem 0.35rem;
    border-radius: 4px;
    font-size: 0.9em;
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
  }
</style>
